    /// Tune in. Starts a playback session for the active profile on what the station plays now.
    ///
    /// The session is an ordinary playback session: every
    /// /playback/sessions operation applies to it, and it ends any other
    /// session of the device. A station session marks nothing watched,
    /// saves no position and counts as no play, whatever position reports
    /// it sends.
    ///
    /// Without live, and always on a music station, the session is on
    /// the one program on now: the server picks its file for this device
    /// as startPlayback does, the stream's positionMs is the live
    /// position, where the client starts, and the client offers no pause
    /// or seek. The program ends at onAir.now.endsAt, which is where its
    /// stream ends. Then the client ends the session and calls this
    /// again: the next program may start at once (always on a music
    /// station, and on a movies or tv station when one ends exactly on
    /// its boundary), or the call answers 409 off_air with resumesAt,
    /// when the client shows the station's identity image and calls
    /// again at resumesAt.
    ///
    /// With live, a movies or tv station answers one stream with live
    /// set: the station's programs one after another, each from the file
    /// the server picks for this device, and the station's ident
    /// wherever the schedule leaves a gap of an hour or less. The client
    /// plays it from its live edge, offers no pause or seek, and does
    /// not call again when a program ends; what is on is getStation's
    /// onAir. Tuned in to an ident, onAir has no now. The stream has no
    /// sidecars and no previews, and a track choice holds for the
    /// program on. It ends when nothing more is on within the hour, or
    /// when what comes next is not for the profile or cannot be played
    /// to the device; the client then ends the session and calls this
    /// again, which answers that program or says why not.
    ///
    /// Errors: 404 for a station the profile may not see. 409 with code
    /// off_air when nothing is on, and with live nothing starts within
    /// the hour either, with resumesAt when the next program starts,
    /// absent when none is scheduled. 403 when the program on now fails
    /// the active kid's filter. 409 with code conflict, as
    /// startPlayback, when the program's edition has no file on disk,
    /// nothing the client reported can play it, or the encoder is busy.
