    /// What downloading the targets at a quality would keep on this device.
    ///
    /// A movie, episode, song or YouTube video stands for itself, playing
    /// editionId or else its default edition; a show, season, artist,
    /// album or channel for its episodes, songs or videos as they are now,
    /// in play order, a channel's by publish date, oldest first; a
    /// collection for its movies in release order; a playlist the profile
    /// owns or is shared for its play order. Titles come once each, in
    /// target order, and only those the profile may see; a target it may
    /// not see answers 404, as one that does not exist does. A request
    /// covering more than 5000 titles answers 400 with the field targets.
    ///
    /// Each title says what this device, as snapshot describes it, would
    /// keep at quality: the file itself when it plays it (direct_play,
    /// sizeBytes exact), else one MP4, or an M4A for a song, that the
    /// server converts (sizeBytes estimated). The snapshot's network group
    /// is not read. A size converts the picture to that rung, never above
    /// the source, with stereo AAC; a size no smaller than the source is
    /// original. For a song every quality but original is aac256: a
    /// lossless song becomes AAC at 256 kb/s and a lossy one stays itself.
    /// original is the file itself, converted only when the device does
    /// not play it, as is aac256 asked of a video. A title with no file on
    /// disk, or none the device plays in any form, is available false.
